2026-10-28T10:42:17.4995436Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4995682Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4995927Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4996198Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4996575Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4996712Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4997036Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4997201Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4997570Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-28T10:42:17.4998075Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5002342Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5002491Z I will:
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5002651Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5003103Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5003688Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5004431Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5005041Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5005324Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5005626Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5006166Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5006595Z    /root
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5018291Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5018815Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5030622Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5031154Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5031583Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5032895Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5033526Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
