2026-10-28T10:42:17.5056566Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5067943Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5068641Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5069359Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5069661Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5069938Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5070303Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5070710Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5071482Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5071938Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5072181Z If you would like to
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5072787Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5073028Z 
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5073241Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5073584Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-28T10:42:17.5073725Z 
